Let $\overline{\mat{
u}}\in \mathbb{C} ^{n} /\mathcal Q_C$, $\mat{\lambda}\in( rac{1}{2}+\mathbb{Z})^{n}$ be a dominant $\mathfrak{so}(2n)$-weight, and $\Sigma \subset {m Hf} ( \overline{\mat{
u}})$.

- [(i) ] There is a unique up to isomorphism simple bounded $\mathfrak{sp}(2n)$-module $S = S(\chi_{\smat{\lambda} + \smat{1}\mat{}}, \overline{\mat{
u}}, \Sigma)$ with central character $\chi_S = \chi_{\smat{\lambda} + \smat{1}\mat{}}$, support $\Supp S \subset\overline{\mat{
u}} $, and cone $\mathcal C_S = \mathcal C_{{m Hf}(\overline{\mat{
u}}) \setminus \Sigma, \Sigma}$.

- [(ii)] If $S(\chi_{\smat{\lambda} + \smat{1}\mat{}}, \overline{\mat{
u}}, \Sigma)$ is the module defined in (i), then every infinite-dimensional simple bounded $\mathfrak{sp}(2n)$-module is isomorphic to some module $S(\chi_{\smat{\lambda} + \smat{1}\mat{}}, \overline{\mat{
u}}, \Sigma)$. In particular, $\mathcal F (\overline{\mat{
u}}, \Sigma) \simeq S(\chi_{\sigma}, \overline{\mat{
u} + \mat{1/2}\mat{}}, \Sigma)$.

- [(iii)] $\deg S(\chi_{\smat{\lambda} + \smat{1}\mat{}}, \overline{\mat{
u}}, \Sigma)  =  rac{1}{2^{n-1}} \dim L_D(\mat{\lambda}) $.
